  "shortDescription": "A community supported campaign to help bring a local foods grocery store and cafe to downtown Lancaster, Pennsylvania.",
  "projectStory": "Project story\nCreator\nRoaring Brook Market\nmore infocontact\nCategory\nLocal Businesses\nTags\nother\nBacking information\nCrowdfunding risks\nlearn more\nWhat are we?\nRoaring Brook Market is a sustainably-minded local foods grocery store and café in downtown Lancaster. In addition to stocking traditional grocery items, we will be featuring local and seasonal breakfast and lunch options in our cafe. \nWho are we?\nRoaring Brook Market is the manifestation of a community-driven food movement. Sarah, Trex, Drew, and Rachel recognized the need for a local food outlet and came together through their shared passion for Lancaster city and belief in the revitalizing power of local food. The market will source goods primarily from within Lancaster and it’s neighboring counties, though our definition of local extends to an 100 miles radius the city. Customers can look forward to seeing grocery items, fresh produce, dry goods, and home and body care products on our shelves, as well as breakfast, lunch, coffee and to-go items in the café.  \nWhy Contribute?\nIn order to make this dream a reality, we need monetary support from the community to purchase the necessary equipment to make a grocery store and café operate. Not only is this campaign a way to bring another small business to Lancaster, but also a way for members of the community to become intrinsically involved in the success of the store. \nWhere does the money go?\n\nBy donating to the campaign, supporters will help Roaring Brook purchase refrigeration equipment from which grocery items will be sold, ranging from produce to meat, to dairy and eggs. In addition to stressing local, we strive to be as sustainable as possible and have chosen energy-efficient models that match our mission.\nWe are also commited to offering our farmers, growers, and suppliers fair and equitable prices for their goods. In order to do this, we need to raise money for our start-up inventory. In addition to paying for equipment, a part of the money raised from the campaign will go towards making our suppliers' work financially viable. \nWhat we need:\nRoaring Brook is on its way towards its full opening but is still short $15,000-$20,000 of the necessary funds for opening. The money raised from this campaign will go towards the purchase and installation of equipment. We are hoping to raise at least $15,000 to cover the cost of the following equipment:\n3-door LED Refrigeration Unit\n3-door LED Freezer Unit\nOpen Air LED Produce Case\nOld Tyme Nut Grinder\nWhat you get!\nMore importantly, what do you get from donating? Besides the supreme satisfaction of supporting a local business, we are offering reward packages for different levels of donation. We appreciate any and all that you can give, and look forward to seeing you in the store!\nOut of towners, please include your shipping address so we can send you your reward!\nOther ways you can help?\nSpread the word! Tell your friends and share our campaign! Find us on Facebook, Twitter, and at www.roaringbrookmarket.com. Or just stop by the store and hang out with us. \n---------------------------------------UPDATE 7/8/13-------------------------------------------\nCheck out our Gallery to see an image of the t-shirts we're offering in thanks for your donations. The shirt is designed by Drew Nowacoski, local Lancaster artist and owner of Roaring Brook, and will be screenprinted by Zach Kolodziejski, a screenprinter also local to our beautiful city. If you purchase a perk of equal or greater value to Wear the Love, you can get your very own Roaring Brook shirt! \n \n---------------------------------------UPDATE 7/11/13-------------------------------------------\nWe've added a perk! Donate $200 (or more) and be an exclusive member of Roaring Brook Market Locavore Club. 10% off your purchases for a year as well as a free coffee everytime you walk in the door. \n \n---------------------------------------UPDATE 8/8/13-------------------------------------------\nThree weeks into operations and we've learned several things--to support our downtown local food mission we need more cold storage, more fresh inventory, and more funding! Check out the coverage from the local news at:\nhttp://lancasteronline.com/article/local/877321_Roaring-Brook-Market---Cafe-opens-in-Lancaster.html",
